Z||000000||fierogt88||05-31-2001||10:34 AM||||I'm moving my battery up front, and I have the box made up.  How much cable do i need to get to make the stretch from front to back?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||05-31-2001||01:44 PM||||A guy who did this conversion used a piece of rope to measure by threading it from front to back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||VISCERAL||05-31-2001||01:52 PM||||Just check out <A HREF="http://www.summit-racing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summit-racing.com</A>  and look at some of their battery relocation cable kits. get their home brand for about $35.oo. cables were about 12' you need about 9 ft'||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||05-31-2001||09:57 PM||||I would rather go to a local welding store. Because you will wind up with better cable. Or a boat store. They also have it on a roll.||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||05-31-2001||10:08 PM|||| Where ya been? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||06-01-2001||07:48 AM||||Autozone carries extra long bat. cables with the ends already crimped on.  I dont know about lengths though, I just noticed they had a display of extra-long ones.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierogt88||06-01-2001||08:29 AM||||I work for an electrical contracting company, so all the wire will be cost-free for me.  I will be using #2 diesel cable, the covering is thicker than the wire itself...<P>I was considering some metal-jacketed cable we have here, but it is extremely difficult to bend.  almost like pipe.<P>danny boy:  I have been working on my resume, and my friend from L.A. came into town this weekend so I spent a lot of time with him.  This past weekend was also the 5th anniversery for me and Bev, so I was really busy.  I'll give you a call.||||reg||1
